Applied on Apple only: stops glib calling pipe2(), which Apple SDKs declare only from iOS/macOS 27.

glib checks its `functions` list with a bare cc.has_function(f), which links against a prototype
of meson's own rather than the SDK's declaration, so it cannot see API availability.  Built with
an SDK of 27 or later it therefore sets HAVE_PIPE2 whatever the deployment target, and
g_unix_open_pipe() (glib-unixprivate.h) calls pipe2() unguarded: a weak import that is null on an
older OS.  Under -Werror=unguarded-availability-new the call is a compile error instead.

Meson has no cache variable to preset, unlike autoconf, so pipe2 comes off the list.  Without
HAVE_PIPE2 g_unix_open_pipe() uses pipe() and fcntl(FD_CLOEXEC), its path on every platform that
lacks pipe2.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -748,7 +748,6 @@
   'memmem',
   'mmap',
   'newlocale',
-  'pipe2',
   'poll',
   'prlimit',
   'readlink',
